     NOTES FOR THE LAKE CREATOR:

   I think it would be best to make it on paper first.  May take a little
 less time.  Use graph paper and make it 15x40 (rows x columns).  Mark
 out the land, the dock (only one!) and use 6 different depths.
 (5,10,15,20,25,30 ft).  If you feel like it, at the same time select the
 different surfaces and bottoms for each block.

   Then you are ready for the creator.  Making a mistake along the way
 cannot be corrected unless you edit the resulting file.  The edit feature
 will be put in the next version. I wrote it quick.  First it will ask for
 a lakename, (20 characters max) then 5 types of fish (MAKE EM ALL DIFFERENT)
 then the mapping routine starts.  Enter the data as you have it on your
 paper OR just do it freehand.

     Once it's done, it'll ask for a filename.  Type in anything.  It will
write a map file to the lakemaps dir and a data file to the lakedata dir.
Rename these to lakeMap# and lakeData#.  Then edit your lakelist file.  
Version 2 will be much easier. I may make an offline file for it.
 (Mouse Driven!)  Your lakelist should have the lakes listed by number
because that's what the program is looking for when the player selects.

   I will start working on lakes, but in the meantime if anyone makes any
 please upload the data file and map file to Future World.  You cannot play
this unless you have at least ONE lake.  To be able to have all 16 fish in 
the game you would have to make at least 4 lakes (5 fish per lake).  So if
you use only one lake, the largest fish caught file will never fill up.

